/*  A nested function stores its own argument into the enclosing function's series.
    Obligation broken: O4, what a function stores into its parameters is its caller's business. See docs/SOUNDNESS.md.  */

Bind void to run-it:
    Define sink as a series of series of number.
    Bind void to tuck, given (the series of number s):
        Insert s into sink.
    Done.
    Pull a rabbit.
        Define inner as a series of number with (1, 2, 3).
        Cast tuck on (inner).
    Done.
    Define churn as a series of text.
    Define tick as 0.
    While tick is less than 400, repeat:
        Insert ("zzzzzzzz" joined to "yyyyyyyy") into churn.
        tick becomes tick + 1.
    Done.
    State sink.
Done.
Cast run-it on ().
